<Base title="About MycoGeeky"><div class="station-page"><section class="station-hero station-hero-split"><div class="station-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT / WHY THIS EXISTS</p><h1>Stay curious. <em>Stay cultivating.</em></h1><p class="lead">You can take science seriously without taking yourself too seriously. Respect expertise without worshipping authority. And contribute to mycology without waiting for someone to invite you.</p><a class="station-button" href="/connect/">Find your people →</a></div><img src="/images/field-photography/mycogeeky-1.jpg" alt="The MycoGeeky host showing a mushroom with humor and enthusiasm" loading="eager" decoding="async"/></section><section class="station-content"><div class="station-section-head"><h2>THE IDEAS BEHIND MYCOGEEKY</h2><span>CURIOSITY / COOPERATION / INTEGRITY</span></div><div class="station-editorial-grid"><article class="tool-card"><p class="eyebrow">01 / LEARN TOGETHER</p><h3>Curiosity over credentials</h3><p>Expertise matters. So does the willingness to ask a good question and do careful work.</p></article><article class="tool-card"><p class="eyebrow">02 / MAKE CONNECTIONS</p><h3>Cooperation over competition</h3><p>Share methods, observations, interpretations, and credit. Help other people contribute.</p></article><article class="tool-card"><p class="eyebrow">03 / KEEP IT OPEN</p><h3>Integrity over opportunity</h3><p>Evidence comes before certainty, and people come before personal branding.</p></article></div></section></div></Base>